    description: "Go module-variable emission (kind=\"variable\") includes function-local `var` declarations, not just package-level `var`. Invariant violated: an emitted go variable symbol must be a package (file) scope `var`, never a function-local `var`.\n\nBehavioral evidence (DEEP cohort deep-20260623-134237/cohort-001/iter-001, caddy): sampled go variable `handler` (replacer.go, inside a test function body) emitted as a module variable. Most caddy go variables ARE package-level (correct, e.g. ConfigAutosavePath, ErrEventAborted, SupportedCurves); the leak is occasional function-local `var`.\n\nRoot cause: var_declaration emission does not restrict to package/file scope -- no check that the declaration's parent chain reaches source_file without an intervening function/block body.\n\nScope: PRE-EXISTING -- predates this session's F5 struct-field slice (go already emitted package vars before F5; emits_variable[go] was satisfied, not stripped this session). Separate code path from the swift field defect, but the same class of bug (scope-level conflation). Lower volume than swift.\n\nFix shape: only emit kind=\"variable\" for var_declaration directly at package (file) scope. Discovered by adversarial ground-truth audit (workflow f5-groundtruth-audit; go PARTIAL, 11/12 variable samples correct). Lab notebook: notebookjournal_06232026_1411.md."  # 8802
    fields:  # 8802
      statement: "An emitted go variable symbol must be a package (file) scope var, never a function-local var."  # 8802
      root_cause: "go var_declaration emission does not restrict to package/file scope; function-local var declarations are emitted as module variables."  # 8802
